KG42.register("clusters-58ab38bb961f82f3fca09976",{"id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::v142-d-CL003","paper":"13-consensus_product_differentiation","label":"Optional participation extension through the splitting of prosumer buying and selling roles","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL003","label":"Optional participation extension through the splitting of prosumer buying and selling roles","market_meaning":"When the prosumer extension is adopted, the buying and selling roles of the same prosumer are represented as distinct negotiating entities linked by internal constraints. The current chain provides the splitting relationship, but has not yet defined internal constraints sufficient to implement the extension or a complete interface with the base market.","mechanism_ids":["M01"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["participation"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"This applies only when the prosumer extension is selected. It differs from the condition in the base model under which each negotiating agent is fixed as either a producer or a consumer. A prosumer's net trading quantity cannot be directly equated with a consumer's requested quantity, nor can a complete sign domain be established solely from positive and negative labels.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"Splitting buying and selling entities involves a new representation of participation and internal coupling conditions. The existing source does not provide a closed interface, so this is retained separately as an extension candidate, rather than being incorporated into the base RCI rules and then declared complete.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R007","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Retain the participation conditions, the two negotiating roles, and the existing splitting expression for the optional extension; keep the missing internal constraints explicit."}],"connections":[],"object_mappings":[],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G001","category":"math_incomplete","description":"Eq. (3) provides only the splitting of the trading quantity. Internal constraints between the two negotiating entities are not provided, and explicit sign domains for the components are not declared in that equation; therefore, the joint feasible set of the buying and selling entities cannot be confirmed.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x2","v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x3","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e08"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Determine whether the source explicitly provides internal constraints and component domains, and then have C supplement them; if the source does not specify them, continue to mark them as missing, without presupposing mutual exclusivity of buying and selling, capacity coupling, or other restrictions."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G002","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The current frozen chain does not map the indices, bids, and reciprocity constraints of the entities resulting from the split to the base market objects. The source also states that the buying and selling roles use opposite criterion values, but this condition has not yet entered the formal constraints of R007; a cross-scope identity mapping cannot be constructed solely on the basis of the shared name P_nm.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x1","v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x2","v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x3","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e08","v141-b-g01-e14","v141-b-g01-e17"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-prop-03"],"required_work":"Upstream must clarify how the indices, sign conditions, criterion values, and reciprocity constraints of the original agent and the two negotiating entities connect, and then propose a cross-chain interface supported by the source; the related coefficient node proposals remain unapproved."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G003","category":"unverified_source","description":"Both the prosumer extension and the statements concerning criterion values constitute candidate evidence that has not been independently reviewed; the current splitting mathematics does not indicate that source verification or implementation completeness has passed review.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e08","v141-b-g01-e14"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the original text concerning the extension conditions, role labels, and internal constraints, and retain the unreviewed status."}]},"rule_refs":["13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R007"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-4fd16cbd90d234cb"]});
